GZIP(1)                   UC.OS Manual                   GZIP(1)

NAME
       gzip, gunzip, zcat, xz, unxz, xzcat, zstd, unzstd, zstdcat -
       compress and decompress files

SYNOPSIS
       gzip [-cdfklnqtv19] [-S suffix] [file...]
       gunzip [-cfkqtv] [file...]
       zcat [-f] [file...]
       xz -d [-cfkqtv] [file...]     unxz, xzcat
       zstd -d [-cfkqtv] [-o file] [file...]     unzstd, zstdcat

DESCRIPTION
       gzip compresses each file into file.gz and removes the
       original. gunzip does the reverse. zcat writes the
       decompressed data to standard output. With no file, they read
       standard input.

              $ gzip -k report.txt
              $ zcat report.txt.gz | head

       xz and zstd here only decompress, test and list: give them -d,
       or use unxz, xzcat, unzstd and zstdcat. zstd keeps the input
       file unless --rm is given.

       Every check the formats carry is verified: the CRC32 and length
       of gzip, the block and index checks of xz, the checksum of zstd.

OPTIONS
       -c     Write to standard output and keep the input files.
       -d     Decompress.
       -f     Overwrite existing files. With -c, data that is not
              compressed is passed through unchanged.
       -k     Keep the input files.
       -l     List compressed and uncompressed sizes.
       -n     Do not store the file name and time when compressing.
       -q     Quiet.
       -t     Test the compressed files.
       -v     Verbose.
       -1 to -9
              Faster to smaller. The default is 6.
       -M SIZE, --memory=SIZE
              The largest window or dictionary to accept (xz, zstd).
              The default is 128M.

SEE ALSO
       tar(1)
